"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released Workflows, a durable, observable, and fault-tolerant orchestration layer in public preview to help you reliably bring enterprise AI processes into production. Workflows are designed to solve problems such as unauthorized termination of notebook-level pipelines in production, network timeouts, and lack of approval mechanisms during multi-step operations. Developers can write workflows in Python and publish them to Le Chat so that anyone in the organization can run them, with every step tracked and auditable through Studio. Efficiently automates complex and time-consuming multi-step business processes such as cargo customs document verification or KYC customer onboarding, waiting for human approval with just one line of code. Introducing Forge Mistral AI has launched ‘Forge’, a system that helps companies develop custom, frontier-grade AI models based on their proprietary knowledge and internal data. Forge lets you build custom AI models by learning internal data, including your company's unique engineering standards, compliance policies, code base, and operational processes. It supports modern training methods such as pre-training, post-training, and reinforcement learning throughout the model life cycle. It is designed to enable companies to run their models on their own infrastructure and maintain complete control and independence over their intellectual property and data. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Through its partnership with NVIDIA, Mistral AI will participate as a founding member of the Nemotron Alliance and accelerate the development of open source frontier models. Mistral AI and NVIDIA plan to jointly develop open source AI models by combining specialized model architectures with computing resources and synthetic data generation pipelines. The coalition's first initiative is a base model trained on NVIDIA DGX Cloud, which will serve as the foundation for the upcoming NVIDIA Nemotron 4 product family. As part of this collaboration, Mistral AI has launched the Mistral Small 4 model to help developers, researchers, and enterprises innovate without barriers. Leanstral: Open-Source foundation for trustworthy vibe-coding Mistral AI has launched Leanstral, a highly efficient open-source code agent designed specifically for Lean 4 proof assistants. Leanstral is an agent designed to not only generate code but also perform formal proofs to solve human verification bottlenecks. Weights is released under the Apache 2.0 license and is available as a free API endpoint and agent mode in Mistral vibe. Using a highly sparse architecture with 6B active parameters optimized for Lean 4 environments, we demonstrated superior performance and cost-effectiveness compared to competing large models. Rails testing on autopilot: Building an agent that writes what developers won't About building a CI/CD-integrated autonomous agent that automatically generates and improves Rails test code not written by developers. To solve the problem of increasing debugging costs due to unwritten test code in large Rails monolith environments, we built an autonomous agent that automatically generates and supplements RSpec tests. The agent recognizes five major file types (models, serializers, controllers, mailers, and helpers), generates tests using type-specific instructions, and performs updates carefully taking into account shared context such as factories and fixtures. This agent is based on Vibe, Mistral's open source coding assistant, and was designed by providing repository-level context (AGENTS.md), leveraging specialized skills and custom tools. Metric-Dependent Annotation Saturation for Learning from Label Distributions This study analyzed that the saturation point of the required number of annotators varies depending on the evaluation index when learning from label distribution. We empirically demonstrated that the number of annotators needed to capture discrepant signals between annotators varies depending on the evaluation metric. In natural language inference (NLI) tasks, the ability of a model to identify inconsistencies (entropic correlation) requires 20 to 50 annotators, while distributional agreement (KL divergence) reaches saturation at around 10. Soft labels convey unique signals for each item that label smoothing cannot imitate, and this effect has been verified in various architectures, including DeBERTa and RoBERTa. NVIDIA Brings Trusted, 24/7 AI Agents to Telecom Operations NVIDIA introduced its security-enhanced communication AI agent platform technology that supports autonomous operation and management of communication networks at TM Forum's DTW Ignite 2026 held in Copenhagen, Denmark. The telecommunications industry is seeking to move beyond simple task automation to fully autonomous networks and operations that autonomously detect and collaboratively respond to problems across network, IT, and business systems. To protect sensitive data, Softbank is leveraging NVIDIA NeMo Safe Synthesizer and Anonymizer technology to create privacy-preserving synthetic datasets and use them to fine-tune communication models and dedicated network agents. Establish compliance and safety nets with NVIDIA NemoClaw blueprints and NVIDIA OpenShell security runtime, enabling autonomous agents to operate safely, predictably, and auditably in communication systems. Why Cultural Awareness is Essential for Global AI This is a study on why cultural understanding and awareness are essential in a global AI system beyond simple multilingual support, as well as the results of a user survey. Multilingual support does not necessarily guarantee cultural understanding, and cultures in digitally underserved areas risk being excluded from AI technologies. Many global users are experiencing limitations when using AI systems, such as having to use English instead of their native language or receiving answers that violate cultural norms. AI may lead to misunderstandings by reinforcing Western-centric perspectives or assuming only the dominant local culture of a particular language as the default. A proof of concept forgives a fragile data path. Operational AI does not. When transitioning AI workloads from pilot to actual service operation, it points out that unstable data transmission paths and point-to-point infrastructure architecture hinder system scalability and GPU efficiency, and explains the need for a powerful data transmission layer. The point-to-point architecture in the pilot operation stage cannot withstand the continuous and simultaneous traffic of an actual operating environment, and the entire system may collapse in the event of a node failure or traffic surge. Delays in network connections and interruptions in data pipelines leave expensive GPU resources idle, preventing effective cost control and leading to poor quality of artificial intelligence output and service level agreement (SLA) violations. In order for an organization to reliably advance artificial intelligence, it must systematically build the data transmission layer of the infrastructure to withstand realistic failure conditions rather than a controlled environment. Top spy agencies say AI cyber threats will impact you within months. Here’s why The Five Eyes intelligence alliance has warned that cyber threats leveraging artificial intelligence (AI) will have a serious impact on businesses and consumers in the coming months. Next-generation AI models such as OpenAI's GPT-5.5-Cyber ​​and Anthropic's Mythos have drastically lowered the technology barrier to hacking, making sophisticated cybercriminals easier. Automated digital agents scan and exploit software vulnerabilities around the clock, launching attacks faster than traditional security patch deployments. Ordinary users are exposed to hyper-personalized phishing emails and data leak threats created by automated systems by analyzing social media. Claude’s latest wobble lands in a worse week Anthropic is facing a reliability crisis due to ongoing system instability, including recent high error rates across several Claude models and outages of Claude Mythos 5 and Claude Fable 5. On June 23, Antropic identified an increase in the error rate of several Claude models and prepared a solution, but did not disclose the specific cause analysis (RCA). Previously, on June 13, the service of Claude Mythos 5 and Claude Fable 5 was interrupted, affecting the API and services in general, and this is seen as a serious signal beyond a simple temporary failure. In a market where artificial intelligence models are increasingly treated like infrastructure, frequent service failures and instability are acting as commercial risks for users and corporate customers. Luminvera bets on immersive software for robotics The story and vision of Luminvera, a Silicon Valley company that pivoted to develop immersive software for robotics. Luminvera initially planned to provide both AR wearable hardware and an AI layer, but recently pivoted to focus only on software for B2B customers in the robotics industry. Based on his experience at Bosch and Mercedes-Benz, founder Lu Yang seeks to improve the inefficient manual process of engineers analyzing and matching 2D flat documents and specifications. Luminvera's software uses AI to convert thousands of pages of text specifications into 3D virtual workspaces and structured constraints that engineers can design with. SpaceX lands $6.3bn compute deal with Reflection AI Open source AI startup Reflection AI has signed a $6.3 billion computing deal to lease Nvidia chips at SpaceX's Memphis data center Colossus 2. Reflection AI will pay $150 million per month to Space Nvidia is an investor in Reflection AI (investing about $800 million last year) and a computing chip supplier, demonstrating the artificial intelligence industry's cyclical deal structure by helping customers who raise funds lease its chips. Space The cybersecurity industry built a $200B business selling you problems. Nobody got paid to fix them. This article points out that the cyber security industry has grown the market for detecting and diagnosing risks, but has neglected the implementation area of ​​actually solving and remediing discovered vulnerabilities, and is about Reclaim Security's efforts to solve this problem. Global cybersecurity spending has skyrocketed, improving visibility into companies' environments, but the number and cost of actual data breaches is not decreasing. Even if a security vulnerability is discovered, actual remediation requires coordination between multiple teams, including IT, cloud, and application, resulting in delayed action and accumulation of backlogs. Reclaim Security focuses on a platform that goes beyond problem detection and automatically resolves discovered security issues under the control of the security team. Astral Systems raises £23M to make cancer isotopes by fusion British fusion startup Astral Systems has secured a £23 million investment to scale up the production of radioisotopes for cancer diagnosis and treatment. Bristol-based Astral Systems has raised a £23 million Series A first tranche led by Mercia Ventures, taking its total cumulative investment to over £28 million. Unlike most fusion companies that promise clean energy generation in the distant future, the company is already generating commercial sales by using its proprietary 'multi-state fusion' technology to generate neutron beams to produce isotopes for cancer treatment. The funds secured will be used to build infrastructure at the former Berkeley power station site in Gloucestershire, with the goal of operating a next-generation nuclear reactor by the end of 2026, launching the isotope market and turning a profit by early 2027. OpenAI launches new initiative to help find and patch open source bugs OpenAI has launched the ‘Patch the Planet’ initiative in collaboration with Trail of Bits to discover and patch security vulnerabilities in open source projects. OpenAI supports open source maintainers in strengthening project security by utilizing Trail of Bits' security engineers and OpenAI's security tools (such as Codex Security). We want to reduce the workload on maintainers by having security engineers review vulnerabilities in advance and help develop patches and tests before they are delivered to maintainers. In the face of increasing cybercrime threats where artificial intelligence identifies vulnerabilities and creates exploits, OpenAI seeks to protect the open source ecosystem by leveraging AI for defensive purposes. Prime Intellect Releases prime-rl 0.6.0 to Train Trillion-Parameter MoE Models on Agentic RL Workloads Prime Intellect has released version 0.6.0 of prime-rl, an open framework for training trillion-parameter scale MoE models on agent RL workloads. By introducing an asynchronous RL approach, we decouple the trainer and inference system and support independent optimization and scaling. We succeeded in training a GLM-5 model on a SWE task with 131k sequence length using only 28 H200 nodes. Inference optimization techniques such as FP8 inference, Wide EP, prefill/decode disaggregation, and KV cache offloading were applied. GLM-5.2 OpenAI-Compatible API: A Hands-On Guide to Reasoning Effort, Function Calling, and Long-Context Retrieval This is a guide to practice functions such as inference control, function calls, and structured output by setting up a client compatible with the OpenAI compatible API instead of running the GLM-5.2 model locally. We build an OpenAI-compatible client and a reusable chat wrapper to use the GLM-5.2 model in an API environment. You can control whether thinking mode is activated and the reasoning effort level (off, high, max). It covers a variety of practical examples, including real-time inference streaming, function calls, JSON structured output, and long-text context search. Here’s Why WebMCP is Exciting An introduction to the concepts and features of WebMCP, an open web standard that allows websites to expose structured, directly callable tools to browser-based AI agents. WebMCP is an open web standard that allows the website to directly inform the agent of the available functions and input/output formats, rather than having the agent guess and click on the UI pixel by pixel. It was jointly developed by Google and Microsoft, and the W3C Web Machine Learning Community Group announced a draft specification in February 2026 and an origin trial was announced at Google I/O 2026. Unlike existing server-to-server protocols like Anthropic's MCP or Agent-to-Agent Communication (A2A), WebMCP handles interactions at the client page and logged-in user layer. 5 Essential Approaches to Robust Outlier Detection We introduce five essential approaches and their respective characteristics to effectively detect outliers that impede data analysis and prediction model performance. The Z-score method is suitable for normally distributed data and diagnoses points with a standard deviation of 3 or more or -3 or less from the mean as outliers, but is sensitive to extreme values. The IQR (interquartile range) method utilizes percentiles to be robust to data that is not normally distributed, and detects data that falls outside the range by 1.5 times Q1 and Q3. In high-dimensional datasets, isolation forest, a machine learning technique that isolates data similar to classification/regression trees, is effective. Shipping huggingface_hub every week with AI, open tools, and a human in the loop An automated CI workflow builder that combines open source tools, open weight models, and human review to shorten the deployment cycle of Hugging Face's core Python library, huggingface_hub, to weekly levels. We have improved our deployment cycle, which previously took 4-6 weeks, to weekly deployments through a single GitHub Actions workflow. Mechanical tasks such as version bumping and tag creation were fully automated, and AI was introduced to draft release notes to increase efficiency. It was designed using only open source tools and an open weight model that other maintainers can run and modify on their own, without any closed models or paid services. How to run GLM-5.2 locally We introduce how to run Z.ai's new open source large language model, GLM-5.2, in a local environment using Unsloth Dynamic GGUF and llama.cpp, as well as the hardware requirements. GLM-5.2 is a large MoE model with 744B total parameters, 40B active parameters, and 1M context window. Unsloth's Dynamic GGUF quantization technology shows high performance preservation compared to size reduction even in extreme compression environments such as 1-bit and 2-bit. You can use Unsloth Studio or llama.cpp for execution, a minimum 245GB RAM/VRAM environment is recommended for running the 2-bit UD-IQ2_M quantization model. Noise Bottleneck: The Subtle Trap of More Information We cover the noise bottleneck phenomenon, in which as more information is collected, more noise than signal, which reduces the ability to understand the situation, and how to deal with it. As data accumulates in large quantities and observation frequency increases, the signal-to-noise ratio rises dramatically. Depending on the observation period, the signal-to-noise ratio varies from 50:50 per year to 0.5:99.5 per hour, and too much information impedes decisions. The important thing is not to know everything, but to know enough, act immediately, and focus on the few things that really matter. Danish privacy activist Lars Andersen subject to police raid Lars Andersen, a Danish privacy activist, was armed and arrested by police for exposing the Prime Minister's personal information. Former police officer turned privacy activist Lars Andersen arrested after posting Prime Minister Mette Frederiksen's CPR numbers and phone number online During the arrest, police cut off power to the router and confiscated Google Nest cameras with local storage, preventing them from obtaining video records for verification. Andersen has been critical of legislation banning encryption and expanding access to personal information, such as police intelligence agencies' DNA registries, but is controversial for his radical protest methods, including stalking politicians' families. Mitchell Hashimoto pledges $400,000 additional donation to Zig Foundation It is reported that Mitchell Hashimoto's family pledged to donate an additional $400,000 to the Zig Foundation, bringing the cumulative support amount to $700,000. The Mitchell Hashimoto family has pledged an additional $400,000 to the Zig Software Foundation (ZSF), $200,000 per year over two years. Hashimoto continues to donate in recognition of Zig's technological progress and philosophy of focusing on quality and independence. Contribution background, Zig's strict no-LLM contribution policy, and the context of Bun's Zig fork/Rust rewrite are discussed together in the community. bigset - What if you had all the data in the world? This is an introduction to bigset, an open source tool that can create a structured dataset on the live web with a single natural language sentence and automatically update it at a set interval. Create a structured dataset by automatically inferring schema (column name, type, primary key, etc.) from the input natural language sentences. Orchestrator agents and sub-agents work in parallel to inspect, verify, remove duplicates, and return the live web to a table. The agent reruns at set intervals (30 minutes to weekly) to continuously keep the dataset up to date. WACV supp. mat. video [R] Ahead of the WACV conference submission deadline, we are asking about the recommended format and length of videos for Supplementary Material. WACV conference paper submission deadline approaches this weekend The guidelines only state that additional materials must be in PDF or ZIP format with a maximum size of 200 MB, making it difficult to know the specific format and length of the video. Additional materials may include videos, proofs, additional figures and tables, detailed experimental analysis, code, etc. What's your biggest pain point when choosing between cloud GPU providers for LLM inference?[R] This article asks questions and seeks opinions on the biggest challenges and decision criteria when choosing a cloud GPU provider for LLM inference. When selecting a GPU provider, we ask which factors to compare: cost per hour ($/hr), cost per token ($/token), throughput, and reliability. Ask whether there are reliable tools or resources used to make decisions, or whether calculations are made manually. The author is a machine learning engineer who is currently doing calculations manually using spreadsheets and was wondering if there is a better way. VibeThinker-3B: Exploring the Frontier of Verifiable Reasoning in Small Language Models A guide to the arXivLabs framework and its collaborative value as collaborators develop and share new features on websites. arXivLabs is a framework that allows collaborators to develop and share new features directly on the arXiv website. The individuals and organizations that join arXivLabs share the values ​​of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv encourages participation from partners who have project ideas that will add value to the community. Sony releases trailer for Taika Waititi's Klara and the Sun Sony has released the first official trailer for the film 'Clara and the Sun', based on Kazuo Ishiguro's novel and directed by Taika Waititi. It is based on the best-selling novel by Nobel Prize winner Kazuo Ishiguro, and was written and directed by Taika Waititi. Jenna Ortega plays Clara, an Artificial Friend trying to find the perfect home, and follows the process of healing Josie's (Mia Taria) family. The cast includes Amy Adams, Natasha Lyonne, Aran Murphy, and Steve Buscemi. How to burst the AI bubble: Strike at its roots Technology journalist and science fiction writer Corey Doctorow has published a new book, 'The Reverse Centaur's Guide to Life After AI,' which exposes the illusions and realities of AI. In his new book, Corey Doctorow tries to separate the hype about AI from the actual reality. In contrast to 'centaurs', which are technologically enhanced humans in automation theory, 'reverse centaur' refers to the phenomenon of humans working like accessories to ruthless machines. A representative example of a reverse centaur is that Amazon delivery drivers are monitored by AI cameras and virtually work as peripherals of delivery trucks. OBD2 'fuel saver' boxes can actually increase costs by damaging your car - do this instead This is a warning that fake fuel saving devices installed in the vehicle's OBD2 port may not actually save fuel, but may actually damage the vehicle and incur greater costs. The ‘Fuel Saving Tuning Box’ OBD2 device on the market is a fraudulent product that has no fuel saving effect. These devices may be nothing more than a blinking LED light box or, in the worst case scenario, they can cause damage to the vehicle's electronic systems. Advertising uses technical terms such as OBD2 and plug and drive and promises absurd fuel savings. I found the best SSD and storage deals for Amazon Prime Day - including Samsung and Kingston In celebration of Amazon Prime Day, we introduce discount information on SSD and storage products from major brands such as Samsung, Kingston, Seagate, and Western Digital. The Amazon Prime Day sale has begun, allowing you to purchase premium M.2 and external SSD products suitable for upgrading laptops and desktops at greatly discounted prices. It provides a list of optimal deals for each brand tailored to the user's various purposes and budget, including games, content creation, and general office work. We analyzed detailed specifications and features of major recommended products such as Samsung 990 PRO (2TB), Kingston XS1000 (1TB), and Seagate One Touch. June Prime Day live blog 2026: We're tracking Amazon deals on SSDs, TVs, laptops and more This article tracks and introduces real-time discount deal information on major tech products such as SSDs, TVs, laptops, and smartwatches in celebration of Amazon Prime Day in June 2026. Amazon Prime Day has begun, and discount deals of more than 50% are in progress in several categories, including tech, and competitors such as Walmart and Best Buy are also offering counter discounts. It offers the lowest prices on popular tech devices, including a 22% discount on Kindle Paperwhite (lowest price this year), Garmin Fenix ​​8 Pro smartwatch, and AirPod Pro 3. For cost-effective home automation, a set of four Kasa smart plugs is sold for less than $25, Fire TV Stick 4K is sold for less than $20, and Apple Watch Series 11 is sold for $120. Prime Day is here - these are the best deals under $50 you can grab right now In celebration of Amazon Prime Day, we introduce the best practical and valuable discount information on IT devices that can be purchased for less than $50. As Amazon Prime Day begins, cost-effective discount deals are offered on a variety of low-priced IT products such as smart home accessories and streaming sticks. Fire TV Stick 4K Max supports 4K streaming, 16GB of storage, cloud gaming, and an ambient experience displaying over 2,000 works of art, and includes one month of Xbox Game Pass. Included in the discount is a 45W Anker wall charger product equipped with a high-resolution touchscreen display that shows the iPhone charging status (power amount, remaining battery level, etc.) in real time. 23 of the best Prime Day laptop deals (I'd actually buy myself) In celebration of Amazon Prime Day, we are introducing recommended, cost-effective laptop discount products. In celebration of Amazon Prime Day, we track and provide real-time discount information on laptops from major brands such as HP, Lenovo, Acer, Asus, Dell, and Apple. The ASUS VivoBook 16-inch model (equipped with Snapdragon X) offers a large screen and excellent battery efficiency, making it ideal for students and office workers. The Acer Aspire 14-inch model is equipped with Intel Core Ultra 5 and Intel Arc GPU for less than $500, showing excellent cost-effectiveness. Why the U.S. Uses Only Half of Its Grid Capacity This is an interview with an organization that advocates technical solutions and policy changes to overcome the inefficiency of the U.S. power grid, which on average is utilized only 40-55% of peak demand. The U.S. power grid is built to meet peak demand, including extreme weather conditions, and the average utilization rate remains at 40-55% during normal times. Demand flexibility technologies such as transmission line current maximization techniques, power transmission route optimization, battery storage integration, and flexible data centers can enable more efficient use of grid capacity. Excessive construction of new power grids causes cost problems such as increased electricity rates, so increasing the utilization rate of existing infrastructure is an economical and quick alternative. AI Is Learning to Read the Room ‘Human-context AI’, a new field of emotional AI research that seeks to comprehensively understand subtle human emotions and environmental context, is developing. Existing emotional AI failed to fully understand complex and contextual human emotions by classifying only one specific emotion through a simple facial expression or voice tone. Human context AI synthesizes various input information such as individual personality, real-time emotional changes, facial dynamics, voice tone, language, and behavior and evaluates them in environmental context. Many companies, including Meta, Hume AI, and Intuition Robotics, are developing and utilizing more sophisticated voice emotion AI through companion apps and conversation devices for the elderly. Microsoft Expands Azure Kubernetes Service with Bare Metal, Fleet Management and AI Infrastructure Microsoft has significantly expanded Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) performance for AI and large-scale cloud native applications with bare metal support, fleet management, and AI infrastructure enhancements in Build 2026. AKS on Bare Metal provides direct access to hardware without a virtualization layer to maximize LLM learning and inference performance through high-performance networking such as NVLink and RDMA. The general availability of Azure Kubernetes Fleet Manager for Arc-enabled clusters enables centralized policy and governance management across hybrid and multi-cloud environments. Error 500 (Server Error)!!1500.That’s an error.There was an error. Please try again later.That’s all we know. Agentic AI: The Weapon That No Longer Needs a Warrior 'Agentic AI', which sets goals and carries out attacks on its own without human intervention, is changing the face of cyber attacks and dealing with the threats and changes that come with it. While AI in the past was an auxiliary tool that helped humans, such as writing phishing emails or suggesting vulnerabilities, agentic AI is an independent actor that makes its own decisions and executes attack steps. The ‘script kiddie as a service’ phenomenon is emerging as even novice attackers without technical skills can independently perform advanced attacks using agentic AI. As multiple unskilled attackers use similar AI models, a ‘behavioral monoculture’ is being formed where attack methods converge and exhibit standardized patterns. NVIDIA unveils robot-specific safety system ‘Halos’… “Safe collaboration between humans and robots” NVIDIA has unveiled 'Halos for Robotics', an integrated safety platform that supports safe collaboration between humanoid robots and humans. Unveiled Halos, the industry's first full-stack safety system that extends the safety technology accumulated in autonomous vehicle development to the robotics field. Significantly enhances the robot’s situational awareness and cognitive capabilities based on NVIDIA’s IGX Thor, Holoscan sensor bridge, and Halos OS. Agility Robotics, a humanoid robot company, participated as the first partner to integrate Halos into the Digit robot and prepare for certification to international safety standards. “AI changes the rules on its own”… Introducing ‘Self-Harness’, which improves model performance by 60% Error 500 (Server Error)!!1500.That’s an error.There was an error. Please try again later.That’s all we know. It is a framework in which agents analyze failure patterns and evolve operating rules on their own without the intervention of human engineers. It has a three-step iterative learning structure: exploring weaknesses, suggesting modifications, and verifying proposals through regression testing. Agent performance was increased by up to 60% just by modifying the harness without changing the model itself. Jifu AI refutes Musk's prediction of 'Chinese version of Misos'... “We will narrow the gap within this year.” Chinese AI CEO Ji Fu refuted Elon Musk's prediction of a performance gap in China's AI model, predicting that the gap with the United States will be narrowed within this year. Elon Musk predicted that it would be the first quarter of next year for a Misos-level model to be released in China. AI CEO Jie Tang Jifu countered Musk's prediction, saying it wouldn't take that long. Zipu AI's GLM-5.2 model showed excellent performance, ranking 4th in the world in external evaluation, leading to a rise in stock prices. Aprila strengthens public institution GPU resource utilization with AI development and operation platform ‘Cheetah’ Aprica has increased the utilization of GPU resources in public institutions and strengthened the efficiency of AI infrastructure operation through the AI ​​development and operation platform ‘Cheetah’. Afreeca, an AI specialist company, is leading the construction of GPU infrastructure for the Gwangju Institute of Science and Technology (GIST) and Incheon Startup Park with its MLOps and LLMOps platform 'Cheetah'. The Cheetah platform provides integrated support for AI model development environment creation, learning management, deployment, pipeline operation, and performance monitoring. Manage limited GPU resources in detail and increase visibility of AI infrastructure operation through GPU split utilization and resource allocation management. Sakana launches model orchestration platform ‘Fugu’… “Beyond Fable performance” Sakana AI has launched ‘Fugu’, an orchestration platform that combines and coordinates multiple AI models to achieve top-level model-level performance. Sakana AI has unveiled 'Fugu' and 'Fugu Ultra', an orchestration system that distributes work to multiple models and derives results after verification. Fugu Ultra scored 93.2 points in LiveCodeBench, a coding performance evaluation indicator, outperforming Antropic's Claude Fable 5 (89.8 points). It has been presented as an alternative to reduce dependence on specific AI providers and secure AI sovereignty, but it is also pointed out that it is a closed model-based service and that high costs are incurred during the orchestration process. Nvidia invests 3.2 trillion won in data center IREN... Building 5GW AI infrastructure together NVIDIA has formed a strategic partnership with data center company IREN to build large-scale AI infrastructure and is investing up to 3.2 trillion won. NVIDIA and IREN agreed to jointly build up to 5GW of AI infrastructure in the global data center pipeline. NVIDIA is granted the right to purchase up to 30 million shares of common stock in IREN at $70 per share, allowing it to invest up to $2.1 billion, and also signed an AI cloud contract worth $3.4 billion. This cooperation is a strategic move by NVIDIA to unite key infrastructure partners and proactively manage the supply chain at a time when securing power and data center sites has emerged as a new bottleneck for AI infrastructure. SK Hynix pursues NASDAQ ADR listing... Up to KRW 22 trillion raised SK Hynix is ​​seeking to raise up to 22 trillion won in funds by promoting the listing of ADRs on the U.S. Nasdaq to respond to the surge in demand for AI memory. SK Hynix is ​​pursuing listing of NASDAQ ADRs as early as late July to early August. The company plans to raise up to $14 billion (approximately 22 trillion won) in funds by offering approximately 2.5% of the total issued shares. The funds raised will be used to secure leadership in the AI ​​memory market by investing in HBM expansion, advanced packaging, and next-generation memory research and development. GSMA MWC26 Shanghai, global mobile community gathering... Mobile expected to contribute more than $2 trillion to China's economy by 2030 GSMA MWC26 Shanghai opens, predicting that mobile technology will contribute more than $2 trillion to the Chinese economy by 2030 and introducing the latest innovative technologies. China accounts for more than 40% of global 5G connections, and 5G-Advanced has been commercialized in more than 330 cities. Mobile technologies and services will generate $1.5 trillion in value, or 7.2% of China's GDP, in 2025 and are expected to reach $2.1 trillion in 2030. At MWC26 Shanghai, innovative technologies exploring the future of connected industries such as AI, robotics, 6G zone, and future constellations will be unveiled. [AI is now] Microsoft, which developed Open AI, has a change of heart... Why did CEO Nadella criticize the ‘AI monopoly theory’? Microsoft (MS) is trying to reorganize the AI ​​competition landscape with a platform strategy that emphasizes low cost and choice instead of exclusive performance competition centered on a few frontier models. Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella strongly criticized the monopoly of data center resources and concentration of power by a few frontier model companies. As Co-Pilot's establishment in the corporate market has been slower than expected, MS is reducing its dependence on a single high-performance model and strengthening its low-cost, multi-model platform strategy. We are seeking to secure leadership centered on the Azure and office ecosystems by converting AI models into replaceable general-purpose infrastructure, including considering the introduction of China's deep seek model. Samsung SDS, LG CNS, Kakao, etc. all mobilized… Public administration is also in the era of ‘Agentic AI’ Major domestic software companies competed to dominate the public AX market by introducing agentic AI and public specialized infrastructure that directly perform public administrative tasks at the public AI exhibition. Agentic AI emerged as a key topic at the '2026 Public AI Expo' in which 56 organizations and companies, including Samsung SDS, LG CNS, Kakao, and NHN Duray, participated. Samsung SDS unveiled its public customized AI full-stack strategy, including AI agent platform 'Fabrics' and B300 GPU-based GPUaaS. LG CNS demonstrated a public AX strategy and security system that combines the agentic AI platform 'Agentic Works' and the ultra-large AI model 'ExaOne'."